    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nMulticursors use the `hl-MCursor` highlight group as a fallback when the Kitty multiple cursors protocol is unsupported, but when the protocol is supported, the color of the extra cursors cannot be changed at all (despite being [supported by the spec](https://sw.kovidgoyal.net/kitty/multiple-cursors-protocol/#changing-the-color-of-extra-cursors)).\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n`hl-MCursor` also works for cursors created via the multiple cursors protocol.\n\n---\n\nWorkaround:\n```lua\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd({ 'UIEnter', 'ColorScheme' }, {\n  callback = function()\n    local hl = vim.api.nvim_get_hl(0, { name = 'MCursor', link = false })\n    local r, g, b =\n      math.floor(hl.bg / 0x10000),\n      math.floor(hl.bg / 0x100) % 0x100,\n      hl.bg % 0x100\n    vim.api.nvim_ui_send(('\\027[>40;2:%s:%s:%s q'):format(r, g, b))\n  end,\n})\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('VimLeave', {\n  callback = function()\n    vim.api.nvim_ui_send('\\027[>40;0 q')\n  end,\n})\n```",
    "closed_at": "2026-09-18T09:26:13Z",
