    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I'd agree that configurable highlighting of extra cursors in Kitty protocol would be nice. However, there are several issues to consider:\n\n- This seems to only allow setting a single color that will be used for both block (full cell) and bar (a left aligned vertical stick) cursors. Those two arguably need different colors: background type for block (to not hide the character underneath) and foreground type for bar (to be visible).\n- It probably needs to be a different highlight groups than is used for highlighting in terminal that don't support Kitty multiple cursors protocol. Otherwise color schemes would be very limited to customizing the multicursor highlighting, mostly due to the above point (making a single fg-bg group work nicely in both terminals is challenging).",
